# collections/Collections.rae — the collections package main module.
#
# Collections are pure-Rae libraries built over the core primitives (List,
# Buffer): open-addressing maps today, and Set / Queue / RingBuffer /
# SparseSet as they are added. Unlike List (which the compiler knows by name
# and keeps in the core prelude), a collection is something you ASK for:
#
#     import collections/StringMap
#     import collections/IntMap
#
# There is no shared runtime here yet — each collection is self-contained over
# core's Buffer primitives. This module exists so `collections/` is a proper
# package (camelCase folder, PascalCase main module) and a home for any future
# cross-collection helper.
